| `make_targets.gate_timeout_seconds` | integer | `14400` | a whole number from 1 to 604800 (a week) | `scripts/run_make_target.py`; `scripts/config_loader.py`; `scripts/resource_limits.py` (`tool_limits`, which refuses an `agents.tool_timeout_seconds` shorter than `make_targets.gate_timeout_seconds` plus twice `make_targets.gate_stop_grace_seconds` plus `agents.tool_gate_margin_seconds`, all of the same tree) | How long the gate runner lets one make run before it ends make's session: SIGTERM to every process in it, whatever its process group, then SIGKILL; a process that left the session (`setsid`) is not signalled. Without `/proc` only make's own process group is seen and signalled, so a process that moved to a group of its own is not. A timeout is red. Raising it needs the same tree's `agents.tool_timeout_seconds` to stay at least `make_targets.gate_timeout_seconds` plus twice `make_targets.gate_stop_grace_seconds` plus `agents.tool_gate_margin_seconds`, or `tool_limits` refuses every agent tool of that tree with exit 14. Optional: absent, the loader's default applies and it writes `[using default] make_targets.gate_timeout_seconds = 14400` to stderr. | one run's limit: `scripts/run_make_target.py --timeout` | always |
